From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nabeel Sowan <nabeel@vibes.se>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 11:12:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] feature: a per-scheme netcfgd network profile, detected
 not linked

A power scheme can now carry a netcfgd profile to switch to when it
activates -- so choosing a battery-saving scheme can trim network
features, with netcfgd deciding what the profile does and tdepowersave
only naming which profile goes with which scheme.

No link to netcfgd: detection is TDEGlobal::dirs()->findExe("ncfg"), and
the work is `ncfg profile list` to fill the combo and `ncfg profile set`
to switch, the same shell-out shape the panel-off code uses for xrandr.
The set runs without a shell so a configured name cannot be interpreted;
the list is read through a pipe because it takes no input.

It is a new "Networking" page in the per-scheme toolbox, shown only when
ncfg is present and removed otherwise, holding one combo -- (no profile
switching) or a profile by name. The selection is stored by name, not
index, so it survives the profile list changing and an unknown name falls
back to not switching. On activation, if a scheme names a profile and ncfg
is present, the profile is set silently -- schemes flip on every
AC/battery change and a popup each time would be noise -- and a failure is
shown as a text line on the page instead, cleared on the next success.

This is a distinct feature from the lid work it currently shares a branch
with, and reads onto its own upstream pull request: it touches the scheme
path and the netcfgd relationship, not the lid. Extract it before
submitting.
